This directory provides users a script "scripts/testPerf.sh" to test the 
performance of TDengine in different situations. Users can do tests on 
different simulated TDengine cluster environments by configuring the
parameters in the script. When the script is executed, a virtual environment
will set up on your computer and data insertion speed and query speed will
be measured. The results will be shown in "../../test_result"


1. The script will generate a "../../build" directory, which contains binary
files to insert and query data from TDengine cluster, and a "../../dnodes" which
contains the data and logs about the dnode. The results are put in 
file "../../test_result".

2. Users can change the parameters in "scripts/testPerf.sh" to simulate the
insert and query speed in different situations. Users can configure parameters
like: numbers of servers in cluster, number of clients to insert data, number
of records to insert for every client etc.

Note 1. This script is better to run in multi-core machines and the number of
servers should be smaller than the number of CPUs.

NOTE 2. After testing, please make sure to run "./scripts/dnode.sh clean" 
to clean the simulated environment on your computer.
